S-r1-2 (RN's half; CH §2.2b's "never authored by CH" is CH's lane to amend to "supplied by CH, derived by none").] The table's key is the ADDENDUM's general form, act kind × the act's category: for PT's composer rows the category is the TARGET's (PT-r1-2's institution rows); for CH's paragon rows it is the act's own domain and side (CH §2.2b), and a target-dependent paragon row reads its target through lens two (CH's "yes" column) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — the verifier's owed note on SEAMS-r1-2]. **THE `body_act` BLOCK** is one more block of this table, keyed (BD's act kind × the body's kind × the target's category), each row the three coordinates; BD SUPPLIES its values as a registration row at its wave through the same registration door, RN derives nothing BD did not register, and the REGISTRATION WALKER pins every act kind BD can mint, so no body act falls to `neutral` by omission (a raid on a hamlet, alms given, a flock sacked) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — BD's routes (`cure/L-BD.md` §4 RN (2): "BD registers its act rows in the inherent-value table (the SEAMS-r1-2 idiom)")]. The walker's closed list is BD's (§3.1): `raided · robbed_road · fought · gave_shelter · merged · escaped · paid_quarter · fed_poor · robbed_quarter`, the six public `body_stance` words, and an army's sack of a flock; the three QUARTER acts are acts upon the town's OWN people, so the town's commons read them through lens two as acts upon themselves (+1 for `paid_quarter` and `fed_poor`, −1 for `robbed_quarter`, × the magnitude band, §6.2's "a holder the deed helped itself reads +1"), whatever the town's alignment — the owner's "good purchase" gang in an evil, chaotic town included; their lens-one values are BD's rows [CURED 2026-10-19 (fp-final r5) — RU-BD-4 · RU-BD-9 · BD §19.0b RN (c)]. **CH's `hunt_won` ROWS** are two rows of the `paragon_act` block (CH §2.2b: a gang or a beast pack `0.70 · 0.65 · 0.65`, admirable; a conclave `0.40 · 0.60 · 0.70`, neutral on its face, its cre